# The PartCAD logo: a skull and crossbones. Four 3D printed PLA plates and one
# M8 bolt, written in the order somebody would put it together.
#
# The bolt is what holds all four, so all four are on the bolt, and each meets
# it differently: the upper bracket is a clearance hole it passes through, the
# lower bracket and the lower bone are tapped and take hold of the thread, and
# the upper bone is a press fit pushed on over the thread between the two.
#
# The two tapped holes are 30mm apart - 24 turns of an M8 coarse pitch - because
# one bolt has one thread and has to find both of them.
links:
  - part: head_half
    package: ../produce_part_cadquery_logo
    name: head_half_1

  - part: bolt
    package: ../produce_part_step
    connect:
      name: head_half_1
      comment: Dropped through the upper bracket, which its head bears on
      toInstance: inner
      how:
        pushForceMax: 5.0

  - part: head_half_tapped
    package: ../produce_part_cadquery_logo
    name: head_half_2
    connect:
      name: bolt
      comment: >-
        Screwed onto the bolt until it meets the bracket above it, crossed with
        it so the two together make the head of the logo.
      withInstance: inner
      withParams: {turnZ: 90}
      toParams: {moveZ: 2.5}
      how:
        turnTorqueMax: 12.0

  - part: bone
    package: ../produce_part_cadquery_logo
    name: bone1
    connect:
      name: bolt
      comment: >-
        Pushed onto the thread rather than screwed along it: the bore is the
        thread's pitch diameter, so the thread bites in half its depth and
        holds it there. That it shares that space with the bolt is not a fault
        - '//pub/std/metric/m' says so on the mating, with 'snapIn'.
      withInstance: top
      toParams: {moveZ: 30.0}
      how:
        pushForceMax: 80.0

  - part: bone_tapped
    package: ../produce_part_cadquery_logo
    name: bone2
    connect:
      name: bolt
      comment: >-
        Screwed on last, up against the bone above it and crossed with it. The
        bolt ends flush with its underside.
      withInstance: top
      withParams: {turnZ: 90}
      toParams: {moveZ: 32.5}
      how:
        turnTorqueMax: 12.0
